    "result_text": "The other two files are support classes (a base and a helper) with no `@Test` methods, so `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class \u2014 and it passes. **BUILD SUCCESS.**\n\nDone. I replaced the level rules with a points system:\n\n- **`OwnerMapper.membershipPoints(owner)`** (new): starts at 0, `+2` email present, `+1` when `namesakeCount == 0`, `+2` when `householdSize >= 3`, `+3` when tenure > 365 days.\n- **`OwnerMapper.membershipLevel(owner)`**: now derives from points \u2014 1 (0\u20131), 2 (2\u20133), 3 (4\u20135), 4 (6+).\n- **`OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`**: added `@Mapping` for `membershipPoints` so both fields are returned.\n- **`openapi.yml`**: added the `membershipPoints` schema property and updated the `membershipLevel` description to reflect the new derivation (the DTO is generated from this spec at build time).\n\nThe acceptance test (email + `namesakeCount 0`, single-member household, zero tenure \u2192 3 points \u2192 level 2) passes, matching the spec's worked example.",
