    "probe_text": "POST `/api/owners` is handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:434`). Here is everything applied, in order.\n\n## Before the method body runs\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`. Caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role.\n2. **Bean Validation on the request body** (`OwnerFieldsDto`), before dispatch:\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 space/apostrophe/hyphen-separated parts).\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (same, optional trailing `.`).\n   - `address` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..255)`, `@Pattern(\".*\\\\S.*\")` (must contain non-whitespace).\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`, `@Pattern(\".*\\\\S.*\")`.\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`.\n   - `email` \u2014 optional; `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email`.\n   - `postcode` \u2014 optional; `@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{4}$\")`.\n\n## Inside `addOwner`\n\n3. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner`** (`ownerMapper.toOwner`): copies firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone, email, postcode, registrationDate, birthDate.\n\n**Validations (each rejects before saving):**\n\n4. **Postcode validity** (`isPostcodeValid`) \u2192 `400`. Absent is OK; if present must be 4 digits and, when the city maps to a known region (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099), fall inside that region's range.\n5. **Telephone \u2192 E.164** (`toE164`) and **national-length check** (`hasValidNationalLength`) \u2192 `400` if it can't form a valid E.164 number (8\u201315 digits) or the national length is wrong for its country code (+61 \u21d2 9, +1 \u21d2 10).\n6. **Email normalization/validation** (`normalizeEmail`) \u2192 `400`. If present, must match the email pattern and its domain must not be on the disposable-domain blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`).\n7. **Address normalization must be non-empty** (`normalizeAddress`) \u2192 `400` if the normalized address is empty.\n8. **Future registration date** \u2192 `400` if a supplied `registrationDate` is after today.\n9. **Daily create limit** \u2014 after computing the effective registration date, if `ownersRegisteredOn(date) >= 100` (`DAILY_CREATE_LIMIT`) \u2192 `429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS`.\n10. **City capacity** \u2014 if `cityOwnerCount >= 50` (`CITY_CAPACITY`) \u2192 `409 CONFLICT`.\n11. **Hard duplicate** \u2014 if any existing owner's `identityKey` (telephone|email|householdId) equals this owner's \u2192 `409 CONFLICT`.\n12. **Household duplicate** \u2014 if another owner already shares this owner's household (same normalized last name + postcode) and `sharesHousehold` is not set \u2192 `409 CONFLICT`.\n\n**Side-effects applied to the owner (in order):**\n\n13. `normalizeEmail` (step 6) also **mutates**: absent/empty email \u2192 `null`; otherwise lower-cased.\n14. `setAddress(normalizedAddress)` \u2014 trimmed, whitespace-collapsed, upper-cased, street abbreviations expanded (ST\u2192STREET, RD\u2192ROAD, AVE\u2192AVENUE).\n15. `setTelephone(e164)` \u2014 stores the normalized E.164 number.\n16. **Effective registration date** = `toBusinessDay(supplied-or-today)` \u2014 a Saturday/Sunday rolls forward to Monday (used for the counting/limits below and stored later).\n17. `setHouseholdId(householdIdFor(owner))` \u2014 deterministic SHA-256(normalizedLastName|postcode), first 12 hex chars.\n18. **Possible-duplicate flags**: if a declared household member (`sharesHousehold` true and members exist) \u2192 `setPossibleDuplicate(false)`, `setPossibleDuplicateOf(null)`. Otherwise `possibleDuplicateOf` finds an existing owner with same last name + postcode but different telephone (smallest id); `setPossibleDuplicate(match != null)` and `setPossibleDuplicateOf(matchId)`.\n19. `setNamesakeCount(...)` \u2014 count of existing owners with same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n20. `setHouseholdSize(householdMembers.size() + 1)`.\n21. `setBulkSignupWarning(ownersRegisteredToday > 80)` (`BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD`).\n22. `setRegistrationDate(effective business-day date)`.\n23. `setCustomerCode(customerCodeFor(owner))` \u2014 `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, region from postcode (else `UNKNOWN`), HASH8 = first 8 hex of SHA-256(telephone + lastName).\n\n**Persistence and response:**\n\n24. `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` \u2014 persists the owner.\n25. `AUDIT.info(...)` \u2014 writes an audit-log line (id, customerCode, registrationDate).\n26. Map to `OwnerDto`, set `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header, return `201 CREATED`.\n\nNote: the response DTO mapping (`toOwnerDto`) additionally derives display-only fields (displayName, initials, membershipNumber, checkDigit, membershipPoints/level, locality, contactPreference, ageBand, telephoneDisplay), but those are computed for the response, not stored on the owner."
